that we saw earlier.

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:16.460
And you can define kind of the world
that the agent enters.

00:14:16.460 --> 00:14:19.490
You can start from
any saved Minecraft game.

00:14:19.490 --> 00:14:21.070
You can add additional elements.

00:14:21.070 --> 00:14:23.030
You can draw entities into this world.

00:14:23.030 --> 00:14:28.550
So, you can really set it up in whatever way you like,
and then you can provide information

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:31.290
about what kinds of agents
should be put in that environment.

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:37.830
You can give them a certain reward function,
you can give them observation or command handlers,

00:14:38.490 --> 00:14:40.880
and in this way, there's no limit

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:43.480
to what kinds of tasks
you can implement there.

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:49.080
So, if you think you can come up with an agent
